    {"id": "u3", "title": "3 · Low class: the sonorants", "intro": "Ten low-class letters with no high-class partner (m n ng y r l w…). A live syllable is mid tone. To give them a rising or low tone, Thai writes a silent ห before them: นา naa → หนา nǎa (ห นำ, unit 7).", "kind": "consonant", "items": [
