    {"id": "u6", "title": "6 · Finals, live and dead syllables", "intro": "Only eight sounds can end a syllable. Many letters share them: all of ก ข ค ฆ end as -k; ด ต ถ ท ธ จ ช ซ ส ศ ษ … end as -t; บ ป พ ฟ ภ as -p. A syllable is LIVE if it ends in a long vowel or m n ng y w, and DEAD if it ends in a short vowel or -k -t -p. Live or dead decides the tone.", "kind": "syllable", "items": [
