      {"ch": "dead · short", "sound": "", "word": "สุข", "rom": "sùk", "mean": "happy (dead, high → low)", "tone": "low"}
    ]},
    {"id": "u7", "title": "7 · Tone marks and tone rules", "intro": "Four marks sit above the consonant. The tone they give depends on the class: ่ (ไม้เอก) → low for mid/high, falling for low. ้ (ไม้โท) → falling for mid/high, high for low. ๊ and ๋ are used on middle-class letters only: high and rising. ห before a sonorant (หนู, หมา) makes it high class; อ before ย (อยู่, อยาก, อย่า, อย่าง) makes it mid.", "kind": "tone", "marks": [
      {"ch": "่", "name": "ไม้เอก", "rom": "mái èek", "rule": "mid/high → low · low → falling"},
      {"ch": "้", "name": "ไม้โท", "rom": "mái too", "rule": "mid/high → falling · low → high"},
      {"ch": "๊", "name": "ไม้ตรี", "rom": "mái dtrii", "rule": "mid only → high"},
      {"ch": "๋", "name": "ไม้จัตวา", "rom": "mái jàt-dtà-waa", "rule": "mid only → rising"}
    ], "items": [
